    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Correlation and Regression Explorations\"\nauthor: \"Arvind V\"\nformat: html\neditor: visual\n---\n\n## Packages\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(tidyverse)\nlibrary(mosaic)\nlibrary(broom)\nlibrary(ggformula)\nggplot2::theme_set(new = theme_classic())\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Intro\n\nI will work through and \"unify\" at least two things:\n\n-   Hadley Wickham's chapter on modelling and his analysis of the linear model for the diamonds dataset\n-   The diagnostic aspects of Linear Regression as detailed in Crawley's book\n\n## Explorations into Diagnostic Plots\n\nLet us create dependent y\\* variables with different sorts of errors:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nx <- 0:300\nen <- rnorm(301, mean = 0, sd = 5)\neu <- (runif(n = 301) - 0.5) * 20\neb <- rnbinom(n = 301, prob = 0.3, size = 2)\neg <- rgamma(n = 301, shape = 1, rate = 1 / x)\nyn <- x + 10 + en\nyu <- x + 10 + eu\nyb <- x + 10 + eb\nyg <- x + 10 + eg\ndata <- tibble(x, yn, yu, yb, yg)\ndata\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<div data-pagedtable=\"false\">\n  <script data-pagedtable-source type=\"application/json\">\n{\"columns\":[{\"label\":[\"x\"],\"name\":[1],\"type\":[\"int\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"yn\"],\"name\":[2],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"yu\"],\"name\":[3],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"yb\"],\"name\":[4],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]},{\"label\":[\"yg\"],\"name\":[5],\"type\":[\"dbl\"],\"align\":[\"right\"]}],\"data\":[{\"1\":\"0\",\"2\":\"10.814749\",\"3\":\"19.092091\",\"4\":\"16\",\"5\":\"10.00000\"},{\"1\":\"1\",\"2\":\"12.568848\",\"3\":\"20.457219\",\"4\":\"16\",\"5\":\"12.67822\"},{\"1\":\"2\",\"2\":\"11.680386\",\"3\":\"3.523174\",\"4\":\"12\",\"5\":\"17.83250\"},{\"1\":\"3\",\"2\":\"4.653279\",\"3\":\"19.836876\",\"4\":\"14\",\"5\":\"14.61869\"},{\"1\":\"4\",\"2\":\"12.391237\",\"3\":\"22.882689\",\"4\":\"23\",\"5\":\"18.45769\"},{\"1\":\"5\",